  "summary_en": "The UK Automated Vehicles Act 2024 creates a regime for authorising self-driving road vehicles, designating authorised self-driving entities, licensing no-user-in-charge operators, and setting criminal and civil enforcement, user-in-charge immunity, police powers and incident investigation. Provisions are being commenced in stages through 2026.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Secretary of State authorises vehicles meeting the self-driving test, against a statement of safety principles requiring safety at least equal to careful, competent human drivers",
   "Authorised self-driving entity bears responsibility for the vehicle; no-user-in-charge operators must be licensed",
   "User-in-charge is immune from driving offences while the feature is engaged, with exceptions",
   "Offences for false or withheld safety information, with up to 14 years for aggravated cases causing death or serious injury",
   "Statutory incident inspectors investigate to improve safety, not to assign blame; civil sanctions include compliance, redress and monetary penalty notices"
  ],
